## The showstopper (S1): abstract coverage claim vs body

Abstract (~L97): "enabling web access and extended reasoning improved
coverage over the memory-only query in only one of the four frontier
agents." Two reviewers read it against two baselines:
- per-agent memory-only baseline (Exp1 same-lab parametric mean F1 vs
  Exp2 naive arm): Mistral improved (≈0.41→0.49), Anthropic declined
  (≈0.67→0.60), Qwen declined (≈0.41→0.37), OpenAI ≈flat (0.63→0.63) —
  claim holds;
- "vs Exp1 best run" baseline: nobody improves — claim fails.
AND the body (~L709-710) explicitly says the Exp2 naive arm "is an
independent sweep, not a re-run of the §exp1 parametric protocol" —
i.e. the cross-experiment comparison the abstract rests on is
disavowed where the data live.

Fix direction (executor verifies numbers first): make the three places
tell ONE story. Keep the abstract sentence only if §exp2 body carries
the per-agent memory-vs-web comparison explicitly, with the
independent-sweep caveat in the same breath (e.g. one sentence + the
caveat clause). Otherwise weaken the abstract to what the body
supports. The abstract is author-polished prose — change the minimum,
and flag the final wording prominently in the PR body for the author.

## Other actions

1. "Degraded vs mixed" (M1): abstract ~L97 and intro ~L150 say the
   multi-step harness "degraded results"; §exp2 body ~L783 says "mixed"
   and omits the per-agent regressions. From tab_exp2_2x2_agents.tex
   (no-docs: Anthropic −0.04, Mistral −0.10, Qwen −0.10, OpenAI +0.02):
   3/4 declined supports "degraded for three of the four agents".
   Align: body states the per-agent deltas; abstract/intro keep
   "degraded" only with the 3-of-4 qualification if the derived table
   supports it.
2. Good-models F1 floor (E2): Discussion states means "0.41–0.67";
   actual floor 0.406. Either reword ("0.40–0.67") or re-derive and use
   whichever 2-dp rounding is honest; prefer extending the emitter to a
   macro if touch-cost is low, else minimal text fix.
3. Scaffolding strip (M3): ~L1631 "revised-prompt rerun in the journal
   version" — an author note promising future work in annex prose.
   Delete or rephrase as scoping without promising a venue (consistent
   with no-promise brief entry).
4. Extensions opener over-promise (M2): ~L830 says each subsection
   "points to the annex that..." but subsection 7.4 (ext-system) has no
   annex. Reword the opener ("most point to an annex" is weak — better:
   drop the universal claim, let each subsection's own pointer do the
   work).
5. Small fixes: ~L677 self-reference "§\ref{sec:exp2}" rendered inside
   §exp2 itself → "this section"; ~L2139 truncated status string
   "Verify ." in the Phase B description → complete or quote verbatim
   if it IS the as-sent string (check the source prompt file; if
   verbatim, mark it as quoted); ~L1076/wherever `fig:coverage-certainty`
   is cited from §exp2 body, the figure now lives in the annex and
   renders as "Figure S2" — add "(annex)" or "Figure~\ref{...} in
   \ref{sec:annex-exp2}" so the S-number doesn't surprise.
6. OPTIONAL nits: orphaned labels sec:intro, sec:conclusion,
   tbl:status-difficulty — harmless; remove only if zero-cost.

